Login -> Menu -> Payment -> Delivery 

Writing every logic in a single program -> Monolithic way of deploying - one single program  written in one single language.

A single program, where all components of a s/w: UI, business logic, data access are build, deploy and scale together as one executable unit.

Advantage:
Simple to manage, monitor and log
Disadvantage :
Huge code, slow in deployment, hard to scale.


Microservice architecture
Breaks a large monolithic application into a collection of small, independent services.
Each service focuses on a single business capability

If we use independent server for each service then we are wasting the resources
If we keep all services in one server then again single point of failure and goes to same issues
We can use multiple ec2 for each service and add a load balancers for each service
If we are using load balancers then there will be hundereds of load balancers

So we can use multiple docker containers for each service

Since we have many services and each service runs on many containers then its difficult to manage
So we use container orchestration tool to manage the containers.
One of such tool is Kubernetes(K8S)



Microservice and containers are made for each other -> they solve complementary problems.

Request of microservice:
	Isolation between the services
	Light weight deployment
	Consistency 
	Independent scaling
Containers offers:
	OS level process isolation using namespace and cgroups
	Containers are also they are in MBs not in GBs
	Docker images are immutable
	each container can scale, start, restart, stop independently.

What is container orchestration tool?
Platform that automates:
	Deployment, management, scale, networking, lifecycle of container. 

"Brain" that coordinates hundreds of containers - deciding where they should run, how they communicate, and what to do if something breaks.

Popular container orchestration tools:
K8s -> Mks(EKS, AKS, GKE, OKE, IKE), docker swarm, open shift, Nomad


CNCF is an organization currently handling k8s.
